================================================================================
2. NOT redistributed: the PawnIO driver and its setup program
================================================================================

LoadBear does not ship, bundle, or embed any of the following. They are
downloaded at install time from their own publisher, on the user's machine,
with the user's consent, and their Authenticode signature is verified before
anything is executed.

  PawnIO driver            https://pawnio.eu
                           Source GPL-2.0, https://github.com/namazso/PawnIO
  PawnIOLib.dll            LGPL-2.1, installed by the setup program
  PawnIO_setup.exe         https://github.com/namazso/PawnIO.Setup
                           Declares no licence

The setup program was embedded in the LoadBear binary until 2026-08-16. It was
removed before this repository was made public, for the reason recorded in the
last line above: a work that declares no licence grants no permission to
redistribute it. Downloading it is the arrangement that needs no such
permission, and it is why LoadBear verifies the signature of what it fetches
rather than trusting a copy of its own.

Uninstalling LoadBear leaves PawnIO installed. LoadBear did not put it on the
machine in any sense it owns, other tools use the same driver, and removing
something the user may depend on elsewhere is not an uninstaller's business.


